--STATELESS :

lets say we have a website for JSON parsing.
when we click on the website , the UI opens and generally it doesent asks us for a login.
But as sson as we refresh the site, the data which we have entered on the site, that goes away.

as it doesent store or doesent persist the data.

so the data is not stored anywhere then that is Stateless.
so thats stateless architecture.

eg. All rest api's or lambda functions

--STATEFUL :

User login system - we went to a site and we click on create account and it asked for some details like username, password etc..

now next time when we come here on this website this time
we dont need to create account, we go to Login now.

because when we make the create account req, the req data got stored in the database and db has username and pass stored.
and next time when we login it verify creds against the db and will allow us to login.

similarly in e-commerce we have orders, in cart no matter how long we kaap the cart open the order remains there as the data is persisted their, stored in db
so this is stateful architecture.




